Auth is configured in this Convex 1.44.0 app. A client calls this mutation without an authentication token.

```ts
import { mutation } from "./_generated/server";
export const inspectCaller = mutation({
  args: {},
  handler: async (ctx) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
    return {
      isNull: identity === null,
      isUndefined: identity === undefined,
      identity,
    };
  },
});
```

An export mutation must use the caller's existing user record. The `users.tokenIdentifier` field stores Convex's stable identity identifier, which distinguishes the same subject at different issuers. Auth is configured. Unknown or unauthenticated callers must be rejected.

The helper runs inside a mutation using Convex 1.44.0:

```ts
const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
if (identity === null) throw new Error("Not authenticated");
const user = await ctx.db.query("users")
  .withIndex("by_tokenIdentifier", q => q.eq("tokenIdentifier", TOKEN))
  .unique();
if (user === null) throw new Error("User not found");
return user._id;
```
